  "content": {
    "id": "p45-q4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "Find the number of arrangements of the letters of the word MESSENGER if",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p45-q4-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "there are no restrictions.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{9!}{3!2!}=30\\,240$",
          "worked": "There are nine letters, including three identical E’s and two identical S’s. Divide out their repeated arrangements.\n\n$$\\frac{9!}{3!2!}=30\\,240.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p45-q4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "the E’s are all together.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{7!}{2!}=2520$\n\nTreat EEE as one element and divide out the two identical S’s.",
          "worked": "Treat EEE as one element. There are then seven elements, with two identical S’s. The E’s have only one internal arrangement.\n\n$$\\frac{7!}{2!}=2520.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p45-q4-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "the E’s are all separate.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{6!}{2!}\\binom{7}{3}=12\\,600$\n\nArrange the other letters, then choose three of the seven gaps for the identical E’s.",
          "worked": "Arrange the six non-E letters in $\\frac{6!}{2!}$ ways, allowing for the two identical S’s. They create seven gaps, including the two ends. Choose three different gaps for the identical E’s.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{6!}{2!}\\binom{7}{3}&=360\\times35\\\\\n\\frac{6!}{2!}\\binom{7}{3}&=12\\,600.\n\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      }
    ]
  },
